From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Subject: [PATCH] apple: admit the J604 on the T8132 J713 handoff

The J604 (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M4, 2024) is a second T8132 laptop. The
Apple 26B123 template ADTs for j604ap and j713ap give the same values
for every node this boot path touches, so admit it per path instead of
forking the J713 code:

- RTKit helper (asc4) MTP keyboard (board.c j713_prepare_input,
  rtkit_helper.c, apple_mtp_kbd.c): arm-io/mtp, dart-mtp, mtp-aop-mux
  and the dockchannel-mtp keyboard node are identical. The only MTP
  difference is the multi-touch hid-merge-personality (C1FD0,5 vs
  C1FD1,3), which this driver does not read.
- Refused RTKit helper fixup (ft_board_setup): the J604 must refuse to
  reach Linux with a half-published session for the same reason as J713.
- Unprobed RTKit helper (rtkit_helper.c): the fixup loop skips a helper
  that is not active, so when probe failed (or the helper never bound)
  &mtp reached Linux as "okay" with no apple,rtkit-handoff and the OS
  rtkit-helper driver would cold-start the MTP ASC. For the J713 class,
  every apple,t8132-rtk-helper-asc4 node that does not carry a session
  kept by an active helper now gets the same treatment as a refused
  publication: handoff claims removed, status = "disabled" (node removed
  if the blob has no room) and the keyboard alias parent disabled. This
  also closes the hole on J713.
- Per-UKI FDT import (j713_fdt.c): ANS/SART, DCP/disp0 and their DARTs,
  the AGX (sgx/gfx-asc), PMP, SPMI, SEP, the APCIE ECAM 0x1cb0000000 and
  the BCM4387 radio (pci14e4,5f72) match. The import now admits a
  short board table, and both trees must name the same board: a J604
  runtime tree is never imported into a J713 OS tree, or the reverse.
  AOP needs nothing extra: m1n1 holds the AOP handoff back on J604
  (aop-target 0 vs 1 is still to be verified), and j713_aop() already
  disables the OS AOP node when the runtime tree carries no
  memory-region.

The table lives in j713_fdt.c because that file is also built as a host
test. The U-Boot side uses apple_j713_class() from t8132_board.h.

Not covered here: the J604's atc-phy2/atc-phy3. The import copies
calibration for atcphy0/1 only, so extra Type-C ports keep USB2 with no
imported USB3 tunables until a J604 tree and an m1n1 capture show
which ports exist (TO-VERIFY). SMP, the SD reader (pci-bridge2) and
the HDMI dcpext path are outside U-Boot.

Tests: test_apple_j713_fdt gains test_j604_runtime_import, which runs
the J713 fault matrix on J604 trees, and test_t8132_board_identity,
which checks that mixed J713/J604 and non-T8132 trees are refused.
test_apple_helper_handoff gains test_t8132_board_handoff_gate, which
compiles the real rtkit_helper_j713_handoff() and apple_j713_class():
J713 and J604 with the apple,t8132-rtk-helper-asc4 helper publish the
mtp-live-v1 session; J604 with another helper, a T8140 board and a bare
apple,t8132 tree do not; rtkit_helper.c has no direct
of_machine_is_compatible() left. Restoring the J713-only gate, or
dropping apple,j604 from the header, makes it fail.
test_j713_unprobed_helper_mtp_disabled runs the real fixup and sweep on
a J604-shaped tree (okay &mtp with the J604 compatible list, DockChannel
HID, keyboard alias) against real libfdt: probe failed, never bound,
stale claims, already disabled, no room for status, a kept live
session, a refused publication and a non-J713 board. Six mutants
(no sweep, no class gate, no keep, live never set, stale claims
trusted, keyboard left enabled) each fail it at run time.
test_helper_reserves_live_buffers now defines debug() and
apple_j713_class() in its harness, so the publish/refuse fault matrix
compiles and passes again. On a macOS host: 18 passed and 3 failed,
against 13 passed and 4 failures at d30213ea plus quiet-console. The
remaining failures are pre-existing: helper_handoff x2 (implicit
debug()/env_get in their harnesses) and mtp_keyboard x1 (linux/input.h
on macOS).

Hardware tested on: NOT YET
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
